==Russian==

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|дитя́}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-дитя.ogg}}

===Etymology 1===
{{root|ru|ine-pro|*dʰeh₁(y)-}}
{{inh+|ru|orv|дѣтѧ}}, from {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*dětę}}. The ''и'' of the first syllable in the singular is from {{l|ru|дити́на}}, nowadays written {{l|ru|дети́на}} by analogy with the accented {{l|ru|де́ти}}, with regular distant assimilation ''ѣ''…''и́'' > ''и''…''и́''. An alternative formulation by Šakhmatov (''ѣ'' > ''и'' before a soft consonant) explains these forms more directly. Ultimately from {{der|ru|ine-pro|*dʰeh₁(y)-}}, whence also {{m|ru|де́ва}}, {{m|ru|дои́ть}}, {{cog|la|fētus}}, {{m|la|fīlius}}, {{m|la|fēcundus}}, {{m|la|fēmina}}, {{m|la|fēlīx}}, and many more.

Compare typologically {{m|ru|сосуно́к}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|ru|дитё||non-standard, partially declinable}}

====Noun====
{{ru-noun|дитя́|n-an|-|
|adj=дитя́чий
|dim=ди́тятко
|expr=дитё,ди́тачка,ди́точка<qq:see {{m|ru|де́точка}}>,дитя́тя}} {{q|see note on oblique forms}}

# {{lb|ru|dated|or|poetic}} [[child]], [[baby]], [[kid]] (also used ironically or in similes)
#: {{syn|ru|ребёнок}}

=====Usage notes=====
* The [[oblique case]]s of singular '''''дитя''''', except for the [[accusative case]], are never used in speech and seldom in modern prose writing, as many native speakers do not intuitively understand their exact inflectional roles in relation to '''''дитя''''', and may consider them strange or even un-Russian. Instead, the corresponding cases of {{m|ru|ребёнок}} are used.
* The plural forms serve as the normal plural forms of {{m|ru|дитёнок}}.

